    {
      "id": "r7r4svy",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Energy"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Energy is the scalar quantity defined as the capacity or ability of a body to do work.",
        "Kinetic energy is the energy possessed by an object owing to its state of motion.",
        "Potential energy is the energy stored within an object due to its position, shape, or state.",
        "The total mechanical energy of an isolated system is conserved if forces acting are conservative.",
        "Power measures the rate at which work is performed or energy is converted over time."
      ],
      "id": "74wk7kd"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a3h5law",
      "content": "• Energy is the capacity to do work."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "n129w7b",
      "content": "• Energy can exist in different forms such as mechanical energy, heat energy, electrical energy and chemical energy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "52vo9qt",
      "content": "• The SI unit of energy is Joule (J)."
    },
    {
      "id": "koa2cmr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Forms of Energy"
    },
    {
      "id": "ofm6kww",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
